<title>UK: Merita Bank sets $150 million structured FRN.</title>
<headline>Merita Bank sets $150 million structured FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merita Bank has launched a $150 million structured perpetual FRN, lead manager Merrill Lynch International Ltd said Tuesday.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $150 MLN  COUPON    *7.00	MATURITY   *PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.557    PAY DATE    30.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.875     REOFFER    99.557    PAY FREQ   *ANNUAL</p>
<p> LISTING    NONE	DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  FINLAND   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  0.50	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALLABLE AT PAR AFTER 10 YEARS AFTER WHICH NOTES PAY</p>
<p>		SIX-MONTH LIBOR +225 B.P. SUBORDINATED OFFERING.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
